## Tutorials

Thedisplayproperty is 
an important CSS property for controlling layout. It specifies whether an HTML 
element is treated as a block or an inline element.

Every HTML element has a default display value, depending on what type of element it is. The default display value for most elements isblockorinline.

Thedisplayproperty is used to change the default display behavior of HTML elements.

A block-level element ALWAYS starts on a new line and takes up the full width available 
(stretches out to the left and right as far as it can).

